; a map with exactly ONE bareword-keyed field. A bareword key is sugar for the equivalent
; text-string value key, so this is a 1-field struct (identical wire shape to the multi-field
; `{ t: uint, u: uint }` form) — parse_group's table detection falls through to the struct path for
; it, alongside value-keys (`{ 0: uint }`) and 2+ fields. Pins that a regression re-introducing the
; old "unsupported table map key (1)" panic would flip this back to PANIC. Positive-output coverage
; lives in the `single_field_map` corpus fixture.
plain = { t: uint }
